# Workflow

Human procedure: `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Current row: `docs/roadmap.md`. Do not name that ID in this rule.

## Order

```text
Grill (when the design branches) → Issue → branch → work → PR → human review → squash merge → retrospective
```

1. Grill when the API, the meaning, or a phase boundary branches. Skill: `.agents/skills/grilling/SKILL.md`. Skip it when the Issue already has acceptance text and that text agrees with `docs/design.ja.md`.
2. Open a GitHub Issue from a template. Blank issues are disabled. One Issue, one PR.
3. A change to the meaning of the spec is a `design` Issue that updates `docs/design.ja.md` and `docs/design.md` together, before any implementation Issue. `docs/design.md` carries the full English text. It is not a pointer page.
4. Branch: `type/<issue-number>-<slug>`.
5. Work that Issue only. Do not start a row whose status is `Set after Grill on #n`.
6. Open a PR with `.github/pull_request_template.md`. `Closes #N` on its own line under `## Related`.
7. A human reviews and squash-merges. Agents do not merge.
8. Retrospective, below, before the next feature branch.

When a decision on an Issue changes (a Grill choice refined in review, a definition of done that moved), edit the Issue body. A comment alone leaves the acceptance text stale.

Each PR sets its own roadmap row's status to `Done` and updates **Current work** to the next row, in the same change. A row is never left `Not started` after its PR merges.

「進めなさい」 is work on an Issue that already exists. It is not a substitute for creating an Issue or deciding scope. History rewrites: `.cursor/rules/git.mdc`.

## Forbidden

- Starting implementation without an Issue number and a branch
- Copying acceptance text onto the roadmap. The roadmap keeps ID, title, Issue, and status. Acceptance text stays on the Issue and in the design
- Writing pass/fail numbers, formats, or file layouts into the roadmap before Grill on that row finishes
- Adding or removing a roadmap row, or editing **Intentionally out of scope**, without Grill → Issue (`.cursor/rules/consent.mdc`)

When a row is recorded before Grill, and the user has named the ID and the Issue:

- ID, kind, title, and dependencies that the Issue already states
- Status is `Set after Grill on #n` only. Do not put the acceptance text on the roadmap

## Stacked PRs

When a PR is opened on top of another, its base is the earlier branch. After any squash merge into main:

1. Merge main into the next branch at once. Do not wait for a review on the old head.
2. A conflicted file the branch did not change takes main's version. A file the branch changed keeps the branch's edits on top of main.
3. Check that `git diff main` lists only the branch's own files.
4. Before pushing, fetch and confirm the PR is still open. Pushing a branch whose PR already merged and was deleted recreates it.
5. Push, and post the new head on its PR so review runs on it.

```text
# BAD — #38 reviewed on a head that still reverted #36's input order
# GOOD — merge origin/main, diff lists classify.rs, mod.rs, simplicial.rs only, post the head
```

## Retrospective

After the squash merge, write three points on the merged PR. Write "none" when a point is empty.

1. A lesson for `.cursor/rules/`, both design files, or one ADR under `docs/adr/`
2. The Issue that will carry it, if any
3. Whether to refactor. Yes opens a `refactor` Issue that is next, before the next feature. Postponing it needs a roadmap row that names when (`.cursor/rules/defer.mdc`)

Draft the three points and stop. Do not file the Issue or edit rules in that same turn. The next feature branch waits until the three points are written.

A correction the user gives during the work, as an ongoing constraint, is still a rule edit in that change (`.cursor/rules/record-corrections.mdc`). A lesson first noticed here waits for the ask.

ADR files use Status, Date, Issue, Context, and Decision. Create `docs/adr/` with the first ADR. Do not keep a retrospective log.

## Gates

The `justfile` arrives with the crate. The names are fixed now.

- `just lint` = `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`
- `just test` = `cargo test`

Cloud CI is not the definition of done until a workflow exists. Do not treat a missing Actions run as a pass.

## Language

Identifiers, rustdoc, Issue bodies, and commit subjects are English. Japanese in the repository is `docs/design.ja.md` and `README.ja.md`. `docs/design.md` is the full English specification, not a pointer. When the two design files differ, follow `docs/design.ja.md`.
